      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested** — Thank you for adding the `RtsUsbBackend` test suite and addressing the edge cases from the previous patchset. Please split the `RtsUsbBackend` interface additions into the prerequisite backend CL and address the remaining test/precondition simplifications noted inline.\n\n### Review Summary\n**Functionality:** ✅ `RtsUsbDevice::dfu_download` properly handles empty payloads, kernel driver detachment, interface claiming/releasing on all error and completion paths, short writes, block status polling, and the trailing zero-length packet.\n**Architecture \u0026 Component Fit:** ✅ Routing USB operations through `RtsUsbBackend` cleanly decouples the DFU state machine from `libusb` and integrates with `utils-test`.\n**Code Simplicity:** ❌ A few simplifications are needed (see inline comments):\n- In `RtsUsbDevice::dfu_download` (`util/rts5817_usb_device.cc`), `find_dfu_interface()` already checks `backend_-\u003eis_open()` at entry and `parse_dfu_transfer_size()` already substitutes `kDfuDefaultTransferSize` when `wTransferSize \u003d\u003d 0`, so the entry checks can be simplified to `if (firmware.empty() || !find_dfu_interface()) return false;`.\n- In `RtsUsbDeviceDownloadTest` (`util/rts5817_usb_device_test.cc`), inherit from `RtsUsbDeviceDfuTest` to reuse `dfu_interface()`, and drop `::testing::Mock::VerifyAndClearExpectations(backend_)` and the repeated mock setup boilerplate in `FailsWithoutOpenDevice`, `FailsWhenNoDfuInterface`, `ContinuesWhenKernelDriverDetachFails`, and `ClaimFailureLeavesNothingToRelease`.\n**Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability:** ✅ Naming, constants (`kDfuDownload`, `kDfuProgressStepPct`), and C++ types follow codebase conventions.\n**Security:** ✅ No security vulnerabilities identified.\n**Testing:** ❌ Comprehensive boundary and failure scenarios are covered, with a couple of assertion/matcher refinements needed in `util/rts5817_usb_device_test.cc`:\n- Assert the exact block payload bytes