      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Code Simplicity (Fixture Reuse \u0026 Avoiding `VerifyAndClearExpectations` Boilerplate):**\n\n1. `RtsUsbDeviceDfuTest` (line 303) already provides `dfu_interface(int number, uint16_t transfer_size)`. Inheriting `RtsUsbDeviceDownloadTest` from `RtsUsbDeviceDfuTest` and using `DoAll(SetArgPointee\u003c0\u003e(...), Return(0))` avoids repeating the 10-line `RtsUsbInterface` construction lambda in `SetUp()`, `ContinuesWhenKernelDriverDetachFails`, and `ClaimFailureLeavesNothingToRelease`.\n2. In GoogleMock, `EXPECT_CALL` expectations are matched in reverse registration order (newest first), and `.WillRepeatedly(...)` expectations without `.Times(...)` have cardinality `AnyNumber()` (0 or more calls). Overriding a single method with `.WillOnce(...)` in a test body works directly without calling `::testing::Mock::VerifyAndClearExpectations(backend_)` or re-registering `is_open()`, `close()`, `error_name(_)`, `get_interfaces(_)`, and `detach_kernel_driver(_)`:\n\n```cpp\nclass RtsUsbDeviceDownloadTest : public RtsUsbDeviceDfuTest {\n    protected:\n\tvoid SetUp() override\n\t{\n\t\tRtsUsbDeviceDfuTest::SetUp();\n\t\tEXPECT_CALL(*backend_, is_open()).WillRepeatedly(Return(true));\n\t\tEXPECT_CALL(*backend_, get_interfaces(_))\n\t\t\t.WillRepeatedly(DoAll(\n\t\t\t\tSetArgPointee\u003c0\u003e(std::vector\u003cRtsUsbInterface\u003e{\n\t\t\t\t\tdfu_interface(kDfuIf, kTransferSize) }),\n\t\t\t\tReturn(0)));\n\t\tEXPECT_CALL(*backend_, detach_kernel_driver(kDfuIf))\n\t\t\t.WillRepeatedly(Return(0));\n\t\tEXPECT_CALL(*backend_, claim_interface(kDfuIf))\n\t\t\t.WillRepeatedly(Return(0));\n\t}\n```\n\nAnd the four setup-override tests simplify to:\n\n```cpp\nTEST_F(RtsUsbDeviceDownloadTest, FailsWithoutOpenDevice)\n{\n\tEXPECT_CALL(*backend_, is_open()).WillOnce(Return(false));\n\n\tEXPECT_FALSE(device_-\u003edfu_download({ 1 }));\n}\n\nTEST_F(RtsUsbDeviceDownloadTest, FailsWhenNoDfuInterface)\n{\n\tEXPECT_CALL(*backend_, get_interfaces(_)).WillOnce(Return(0));\n\tEXPECT_CALL(*backend_, claim_interface(_)).Times(0);\n\n\tEXPECT_FALSE(device_-\u003edfu_download({ 1 }));\n}\n\nTEST_F(RtsUsbDeviceDownloadTest, ContinuesWhenKernelDriverDetachFails)\n{\n\tEXPECT_CALL(*backend_, detach_kernel_driver(kDfuIf))\n\t\t.WillOnce(Return(-1));\n\trecord_downloads();\n\tstatus_always_idle();\n\tEXPECT_CALL(*backend_, release_interface(kDfuIf));\n\n\tEXPECT_TRUE(device_-\u003edfu_download({ 1, 2 }));\n}\n\nTEST_F(RtsUsbDeviceDownloadTest, ClaimFailureLeavesNothingToRelease)\n{\n\tEXPECT_CALL(*backend_, claim_interface(kDfuIf)).WillOnce(Return(-1));\n\tEXPECT_CALL(*backend_, release_interface(_)).Times(0);\n\n\tEXPECT_FALSE(device_-\u003edfu_download({ 1, 2 }));\n}\n```\n\nOther locations in this file:\n- **Lines 739–747** (`FailsWithoutOpenDevice`)\n- **Lines 749–759** (`FailsWhenNoDfuInterface`)\n- **Lines 761–786** (`ContinuesWhenKernelDriverDetachFails`)\n- **Lines 788–811** (`ClaimFailureLeavesNothingToRelease`)\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/c4d18987-0543-4539-89be-1c0e912698a4)",
